'' A STRING RVALUE PASSED AS AN ARGUMENT, in the three shapes functions/temp-strings
'' writes side by side. Measured:
''
''   byval as string   a caller-built descriptor, assigned into and deleted after
''   zstring ptr       the same temporary, read one level further: '*(char**)&TMP'
''   wstring ptr       the wide value IS the pointer: 'TMP = fb_WstrHex_l( 255 )'
''
'' A WIDE argument to a NARROW parameter is CONVERTED, not reinterpreted: measured,
'' 'takeZstringPtr( w )' is 'fb_WstrAssignToA( &TMP, -1, (uint16*)W, 0 )' and then
'' '*(char**)&TMP'. tiko loaded the wide buffer's address and bitcast it, so the
'' callee read UTF-16 as bytes -- and nothing declined.
''
'' And the radix family had NO TYPE AT ALL -- measured with '#print typeof', hex/oct/
'' bin are STRING and whex/woct/wbin are 'WSTRING * 1' -- so every call taking one as
'' an argument reached overload resolution with an untyped argument and resolved to
'' nothing.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/string-temp-args.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/string-temp-args.out
